From: dash kernel maintainers <dash@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] tools/lib/bpf: match strchr result with const input

The fixed AOSP clang r510928 treats the strchr() result as const when its
input is const.  libbpf stored that result in a non-const pointer, which
breaks the host resolve_btfids build with -Werror.  The pointer is only
used for address arithmetic and a read-only lookup, so keep it const.

This is a host-tool build fix and does not change kernel or BPF ABI.
---
 tools/lib/bpf/libbpf.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tools/lib/bpf/libbpf.c b/tools/lib/bpf/libbpf.c
index 95f2ffeff..802ae6dbd 100644
--- a/tools/lib/bpf/libbpf.c
+++ b/tools/lib/bpf/libbpf.c
@@ -11247,7 +11247,7 @@ static int resolve_full_path(const char *file, char *result, size_t result_sz)
 		if (!search_paths[i])
 			continue;
 		for (s = search_paths[i]; s != NULL; s = strchr(s, ':')) {
-			char *next_path;
+			const char *next_path;
 			int seg_len;
 
 			if (s[0] == ':')
